music BGM26B.mp3
text We place the final parts into the head, the "eyes."
text Now, the junk-doll is complete.
text ..."Done!"
text The girl lies down and stretches her tired limbs.
text I stay in place, facing the doll in anticipation for it to begin moving.
text It's a clumsy, misshapen figure, sure.
text Its arms are of different lengths, and the bottom of its mouth is protruding.
text What a funny face.
text Nevertheless, it's a new friend; someone to be a companion with.
text So I'll just have to ignore the fact that it looks a little silly.
text I keep waiting.
text My new companion doesn't move though, even after waiting for a while.
text ......
text The girl sits up from the floor.
text She joins me in looking at the unmoving doll.
text Perhaps we need to do something special to make it start moving.
text I try to remember the first thing I did.
text That's right. I practiced walking.
text Since this is my friend, I feel as though I need to be the first one to teach it this.
text So that's what I'll do.
text I walk a short distance away from it and clap my hands, just as she once did for me.
text It's a signal that even a newborn can understand: come here.
text My hands make a dull thunk as I clap them together.
text ......
text *Thunk* *Thunk*
text ......
text The doll makes no attempt to stand.
text *Thunk* *Thunk*
text I continue to clap my hands together.
text Still, it shows no signs of engaging.
text Its head hangs low, almost as if dead.
text *Thunk* *Thunk*
text ......
text The girl is now looking at me as I clap my hands. I don't know how long she's been watching.
text She slides over on her knees, then hugs me with so much force that I almost fall over.
text And then, she cries.
text ..."I'm sorry. I'm sorry."
text She repeats the words again and again.
music ~
